new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9811474
--- /dev/null
+++ b/keystore2/tests/integrity_monitor_model/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@
+# TEE monitor renewal review and model
+
+2026-10-31. Host-only specification of the optimization in the AOSP consumer,
+not ASTER collection/classification. This Python model is not imported by
+production code. A separate production Rust decision layer and build target
+have now been added, as described below. Ordinary existing-key signing/decryption
+and historical certificates are outside this monitor's revocation scope.
+
+Run from the workspace root (Python 3.10+):
+
+```sh
+python3 -B system/security/keystore2/tests/integrity_monitor_model/test_model.py
+```
+
+## Source audit
+
+- `src/integrity_policy.rs`: a single monitor owns both property writes. It
+  samples every 250ms, publishes `tee_status` with BOOTTIME + 2000ms, and writes
+  a stopped ACK only if `permit()` is absent and a fresh ACTIVE load is zero.
+  Successful empty ACK clearing is already cached; nonempty ACK/status renewal
+  currently is not. There are no new timers, threads or property writers here.
+- `GenerationGuard` increments ACTIVE before admission, rechecks the permit,
+  decrements on drop and checks the current identity before customized result
+  storage in `security_level.rs`. This optimization must not change those checks.
+- `PlatformIntegrityService.java:teeHeartbeat/teeStopped` binds identity and
+  instance and accepts only `0 < deadline - elapsedRealtime <= 2000ms`. Status
+  allows either activity bit; ACK requires zero. The two properties are read
+  separately and do not form an atomic pair.
+- `device/lineage/sepolicy/common/private/property_contexts` labels both
+  properties `platform_integrity_tee_ack_prop`. The corresponding
+  `platform_integrity.te` grants keystore set/get through `set_prop` and
+  system_server get. No new property, domain, access grant or collector fd is
+  needed. This is source policy review, not effective-policy device acceptance.
+
+The live loop reads policy and ACTIVE more than once. Those reads can disagree
+when the policy changes or an operation begins/ends. The model accepts an
+already-validated sampled Context; it does not claim to remove those races.
+Before production integration, obtain the identity/permit relationship from
+validated input and recheck identity, permit and ACTIVE when committing a write
+or deciding to skip. Do not accidentally unify the existing independent samples
+in a way that publishes a stopped ACK from stale ACTIVE or a different identity.
+If inputs changed, invalidate the decision and retry on a later check, without
+an unbounded retry loop. Ordinary four-second permit renewal with unchanged
+identity and permission need not force a TEE renewal.
+
+## Proposed rules
+
+Each property has its own successful-write state. Renew a 2000ms record when
+remaining time is **at most 1000ms**. The regular 250ms check remains. This leaves
+approximately one second of freshness reserve at the renewal point under normal
+scheduling; it does not guarantee availability through arbitrary scheduling or
+property-service stalls.
+
+On a sampled identity, instance, permission or activity transition, invalidate
+both cached successes and write the required new state on this check. Status
+continues to write on every check while activity is nonzero. A stopped ACK is
+cleared when permission is present or activity is nonzero. Empty clearing may
+be skipped only after successful clearing and an actual-value comparison.
+Invalid/unreadable policy invalidates local renewal state and issues no old-
+identity renewal; already-published values retain their original expiry. It
+does not create a stop ACK or claim the prior values instantly disappeared.
+
+Before skipping any write, compare the actual property with this instance's
+last successful value. Replacement, absence or read failure forces the write
+path; failed writes never update successful state. Status and ACK failures are
+independent. Readback followed by a skip is not atomic with another writer and
+does not establish tamper resistance against a compromised kernel/property
+service. The current trust boundary is unchanged.
+
+Plans bind context and generation; late completion after a sampled transition
+cannot populate the new success cache. An expired write cannot receive a fresh
+deadline just because it returned successfully. Clock failure, regression or
+overflow invalidates state; this model requires a fresh monitor after clock
+failure. These are proposed guards, not claims about current production code.
+The loop remains a single writer: do not add an asynchronous publisher merely
+to implement the model's completion token. It cannot undo an already-written
+property, prevent an indefinitely blocked set, or manufacture an atomic state
+transition across two properties.
+
+## Coverage and limits
+
+24 tests cover stable renewal and exact margin, each context change, active
+work, stop/drain/clear, independent and partial write failures, actual-value
+replacement/read errors, invalid policy, restart, expiry across sleep, clock
+failure/regression, stale/observed-ABA completion and existing consumer limits.
+The consumer helper tests valid-format records; it is not an alternative full
+wire parser. Production Java/Rust tests are still needed for integration.
+
+At perfect 250ms scheduling over four seconds the model writes each nonempty
+stable property four times, versus sixteen per-check writes. This **75% modeled
+write reduction** is not a measured CPU, wakeup or energy reduction. The number
+of monitor checks is unchanged. In permitted idle state the ACK is empty and
+already benefits from the prior clear optimization; do not count it again.
+
+Tradeoffs remain: less remaining validity during some checks, and write-channel
+failure discovered at the next real renewal or transition instead of every
+250ms. Invalid input or readback may increase writes rather than saving work.
+The model does not fix prior unobserved ACTIVE ABA or permit-change races;
+sampling cannot prove that no customized operation ran between checks. Failed
+clear can leave a previously published ACK until its deadline; this existing
+two-property limitation is not a new successful stop confirmation.
+
+Before landing runtime changes: translate this small decision layer into Rust
+tests with injected clock/property results, review sample/commit ordering and
+failed clear behavior, then let the maintainer build. Device validation must
+cover positive and restricted paths, real renewal spacing, transitions and
+failures. No property deadline, normal/compromise policy, ASTER evidence,
+notification, proc format/publication or FAS executor is changed by this model.
+
+## Rust implementation added; maintainer build pending
+
+`src/integrity_monitor.rs` now contains the synchronous decision layer used by
+`src/integrity_policy.rs`. Android-specific property/clock/ACTIVE access remains
+in `MonitorIo`; the decision layer receives injected I/O and is compiled directly
+by the standalone host target, without keystore HAL/database dependencies.
+
+23 Rust tests in `src/integrity_monitor_tests.rs` cover the actual decision code,
+including policy/activity change before status set, after set, before ACK set,
+after ACK set, and before a cached skip. These tests have **not been compiled or
+run by the agent**. Python's 24 reference-model tests still pass. Rustfmt parsing
+and Git whitespace checks pass; those are not a Rust type check or Soong build.
+
+The adapter now derives permit eligibility and identity from the same parsed
+policy instead of pairing an earlier identity with a separate `permit()` read.
+The layer reads the actual channel value, rechecks a fresh sample before either
+skip or set, and samples again after each set before saving success. A detected
+mid-round change invalidates caches and defers remaining publication until the
+next regular check, with no spin/retry loop. State changes already visible at
+the start of a tick force publication in that tick. A set already sent cannot
+be recalled; previously published ACKs still have their original expiry. This
+does not close unobserved ABA or guarantee an atomic stop transaction.
+
+The BOOTTIME helper now checks invalid timespec fields and arithmetic overflow.
+Invalid/regressing monitor clocks stop renewal rather than wrapping a deadline;
+ordinary permit admission still rejects the failure sentinel. Guard admission
+and customized-result commit code are unchanged. The 250ms sleep, consumers,
+wire format, SELinux, ASTER and FAS runtime code are unchanged.
+
+Maintainer validation commands:
+
+```sh
+m aster_tee_monitor_test keystore2
+out/host/linux-x86/nativetest64/aster_tee_monitor_test/aster_tee_monitor_test
+```
+
+The Rust test target is in `keystore2/Android.bp`; it is not packaged into the
+product. Build/run the test and verify all 23 cases before product build/flash.
+Then validate real status/ACK expiry, state transitions, identity changes,
+failures and suspend; measure CPU/observer cost rather than assuming fewer sets
+offset the additional local property reads. No on-device validation was done
+for this change, and a blocking Android property set still has no new bound.
